<question type="multichoice">
  <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_EVOLUTION_DIAGRAM_Q01 - Miller spark discharge apparatus and chemical evolution</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
    <p>The schematic diagram below represents S.L. Miller's 1953 experiment simulating early Earth conditions.</p>
    <p><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 520 340" width="520" height="340" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #d0d7de;border-radius:6px;">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="520" height="340" fill="#ffffff"/>
      <!-- Boiling water flask -->
      <circle cx="110" cy="255" r="36" fill="#d8e9f8" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="110" y="252" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">Boiling</text>
      <text x="110" y="266" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">water</text>
      <!-- Left vertical tube to spark chamber -->
      <path d="M 104 219 L 104 42 L 295 42 L 295 66" fill="none" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <path d="M 116 219 L 116 54 L 283 54 L 283 66" fill="none" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <!-- Vacuum pump branch -->
      <path d="M 104 115 L 65 115" fill="none" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <path d="M 104 125 L 65 125" fill="none" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="34" y="103" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">To vacuum</text>
      <text x="34" y="117" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">pump</text>
      <!-- Spark discharge chamber -->
      <circle cx="289" cy="118" r="52" fill="#e5e7eb" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <!-- Electrodes -->
      <line x1="255" y1="48" x2="279" y2="105" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <circle cx="255" cy="48" r="4" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <line x1="323" y1="48" x2="299" y2="105" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <circle cx="323" cy="48" r="4" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="360" y="52" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#111827">Electrodes</text>
      <!-- Spark -->
      <polygon points="289,94 295,108 310,104 298,116 308,128 293,124 289,138 285,124 270,128 280,116 268,104 283,108" fill="#fbbf24" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1"/>
      <text x="385" y="114" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#111827">Spark</text>
      <text x="385" y="128" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#111827">discharge (800°C)</text>
      <!-- Label X for gases -->
      <text x="200" y="118" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#b91c1c">X</text>
      <line x1="214" y1="114" x2="250" y2="114" stroke="#b91c1c" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3,2"/>
      <!-- Condenser -->
      <rect x="275" y="182" width="28" height="62" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <line x1="289" y1="170" x2="289" y2="262" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <line x1="303" y1="194" x2="328" y2="194" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <line x1="303" y1="232" x2="328" y2="232" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="335" y="198" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Water out</text>
      <text x="335" y="216" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#111827">Condenser</text>
      <text x="335" y="236" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#111827">Water in</text>
      <!-- U-trap -->
      <path d="M 146 255 L 185 255 L 185 295 Q 237 315 289 295 L 289 262" fill="none" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <path d="M 144 265 L 175 265 L 175 300 Q 237 325 299 300 L 299 262" fill="none" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="237" y="330" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">Liquid water in trap (<tspan font-weight="bold" fill="#b91c1c">Y</tspan>)</text>
      <!-- Flow arrows -->
      <text x="92" y="170" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" fill="#374151">↑</text>
      <text x="262" y="176" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" fill="#374151">↓</text>
    </svg></p>
    <p>Identify the gas mixture <strong>X</strong> introduced into the spark-discharge chamber and the key organic compounds subsequently detected in the liquid water trap <strong>Y</strong>.</p>
  ]]></text></questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
    <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The diagram shows S.L. Miller's closed-flask spark-discharge apparatus: a boiling water flask at the bottom left supplies water vapour to an upper spark-discharge chamber fitted with electrodes operating at \(800^\circ\text{C}\), followed by a water-cooled condenser and a U-shaped liquid water trap at the bottom. Region X denotes the gases inside the spark chamber, and region Y denotes the condensed liquid in the trap.</p>
    <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Biological Model</strong><br/>Miller aimed to replicate the reducing atmosphere of primitive Earth, which lacked free molecular oxygen (\(O_2\)) and was characterised by high temperature and electrical discharges (lightning).</p>
    <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Principles</strong><br/>According to the Oparin-Haldane hypothesis of chemical evolution, inorganic gases under reducing conditions and high energy form simple organic monomers such as amino acids.</p>
    <p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>In Miller's 1953 experiment, the closed flask contained methane (\(CH_4\)), hydrogen (\(H_2\)), ammonia (\(NH_3\)), and water vapour (\(H_2O\)) at \(800^\circ\text{C}\). After passing an electric discharge through this gas mixture and condensing the products into the trap, Miller observed the formation of amino acids in the collected water.</p>
    <p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>Free oxygen (\(O_2\)) was absent in Miller's apparatus because early Earth's atmosphere was reducing. Therefore, X corresponds to \(CH_4, NH_3, H_2,\) and \(H_2O\) vapour, and Y yielded amino acids.</p>
  ]]></text></generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
