<question type="multichoice">
  <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_EVOLUTION_DIAGRAM_Q03 - Evolutionary history of vertebrates sauropsids synapsids</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
    <p>The cladogram below shows a simplified evolutionary history of vertebrates from early reptiles.</p>
    <p><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 520 300" width="520" height="300" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #d0d7de;border-radius:6px;">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="520" height="300" fill="#ffffff"/>
      <!-- Early reptiles -->
      <rect x="195" y="252" width="130" height="30" rx="5" fill="#fde68a" stroke="#b45309" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="260" y="271" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">Early reptiles (extinct)</text>
      <!-- Main split -->
      <line x1="260" y1="252" x2="260" y2="225" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <line x1="140" y1="225" x2="395" y2="225" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <!-- Sauropsids branch -->
      <line x1="140" y1="225" x2="140" y2="195" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <rect x="90" y="170" width="100" height="26" rx="4" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#b45309" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="140" y="187" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">Sauropsids</text>
      <!-- Sauropsids to Turtles & Thecodonts -->
      <line x1="140" y1="170" x2="140" y2="145" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <line x1="65" y1="145" x2="230" y2="145" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <line x1="65" y1="145" x2="65" y2="55" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <text x="65" y="42" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">Turtles</text>
      <line x1="230" y1="145" x2="230" y2="120" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <rect x="175" y="94" width="110" height="26" rx="4" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#b45309" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="230" y="111" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">Thecodonts</text>
      <!-- Thecodonts to Crocodiles, Dinosaurs, X -->
      <line x1="230" y1="94" x2="230" y2="72" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <line x1="145" y1="72" x2="310" y2="72" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <line x1="145" y1="72" x2="145" y2="55" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <text x="145" y="42" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">Crocodiles</text>
      <line x1="230" y1="72" x2="230" y2="55" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <text x="230" y="42" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">Dinosaurs (extinct)</text>
      <line x1="310" y1="72" x2="310" y2="55" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <text x="310" y="42" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b91c1c">X</text>
      <!-- Synapsids branch -->
      <line x1="395" y1="225" x2="395" y2="195" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <rect x="345" y="170" width="100" height="26" rx="4" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#b45309" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="395" y="187" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">Synapsids</text>
      <!-- Synapsids -> Pelycosaurs -> Therapsids -> Y -->
      <line x1="395" y1="170" x2="395" y2="148" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <rect x="345" y="122" width="100" height="26" rx="4" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#b45309" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="395" y="139" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">Pelycosaurs</text>
      <line x1="395" y1="122" x2="395" y2="100" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <rect x="345" y="74" width="100" height="26" rx="4" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#b45309" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="395" y="91" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111827">Therapsids</text>
      <line x1="395" y1="74" x2="395" y2="55" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>
      <text x="395" y="42" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b91c1c">Y</text>
    </svg></p>
    <p>Identify the extant vertebrate groups represented by <strong>X</strong> and <strong>Y</strong>.</p>
  ]]></text></questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
    <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The cladogram traces two major evolutionary lineages diverging from extinct early reptiles: the Sauropsids branch on the left and the Synapsids branch on the right. On the Sauropsids side, Thecodonts give rise to Crocodiles, extinct Dinosaurs, and X. On the Synapsids side, Pelycosaurs give rise to Therapsids, which lead to Y.</p>
    <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Biological Model</strong><br/>The branching diagram represents the evolutionary history of amniote vertebrates through geological periods, where nodes indicate ancestral groups and terminal branches represent extinct or modern-day descendants.</p>
    <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Principles</strong><br/>Early reptiles diverged into two major lineages: Sauropsids (leading to modern reptiles and birds) and Synapsids (leading to mammals).</p>
    <p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>- Following the Sauropsids lineage, Thecodonts gave rise to dinosaurs, crocodiles, and <strong>Birds</strong> (X).<br/>- Following the Synapsids lineage, Pelycosaurs evolved into Therapsids, which ultimately gave rise to <strong>Mammals</strong> (Y).</p>
    <p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>Thus, X represents Birds and Y represents Mammals.</p>
  ]]></text></generalfeedback>
