<question type="multichoice">
  <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_EVOLUTION_DIAGRAM_Q04 - Homologous forelimb bone pattern in mammals</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
    <p>The schematic diagram below represents the shared anatomical bone pattern found in the forelimbs of mammals such as humans, cheetahs, whales, and bats, with three segments labelled <strong>1</strong>, <strong>2</strong>, and <strong>3</strong> from proximal to distal.</p>
    <p><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 280" width="420" height="280" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #d0d7de;border-radius:6px;">
